From 70fb4668df293fb7f0811e50909533f010c07c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:10:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: build Move A/B/C offensive playbook
 (schema/wikidata, press outreach, reddit ramp)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ports mcs/cms's offensive/ templates alongside the existing defensive
monitoring skills. Three new tables (rep_offensive_checklist,
rep_pitch_targets, rep_reddit_ramp) plus server logic, API routes, and
a dedicated UI surface under a client's engagement page.

Every move only generates, drafts, or tracks — never sends an email or
posts to Reddit on the operator's behalf, per the templates' own
outreach-authenticity and anti-automation guidance:
  - Move A generates a Schema.org JSON-LD graph and a Wikidata
    statements guide from the client's identity graph, for manual
    deployment/submission.
  - Move B manages a Tier-1 press target list, drafts pitch copy via
    Claude across three archetypes, and tracks outreach history.
  - Move C tracks a 90-day Reddit ramp (handle, subreddit tiering,
    activity log) with pure calculators for ramp phase and the
    karma/account-age gate table — no Reddit credentials are ever held.

This closes out the Reputation Manager build-out arc alongside the
already-committed Counter Claim stub cleanup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
